# The signed approvals step, part: fixes from the permission path's review
# (docs/steps/signed-approvals/parts/review-fixes-core.md), and the two of
# the system layer's review that are in the reset. What a store pins
# restricts under --trust-project too, and while the user's pins do not
# count; nothing another program does blocks the person's reset; a key
# signs only when it opens the key file and is the open key; a question is
# put only with a proposal from its own reading, three times at most; a yes
# signs only its own project's trust.

# ---------------------------------------- what restricts under --trust-project

[break] trust-project-reads-no-entry
rule: Under --trust-project the project's entry is read with the session's key, so that what an entry that does not count pins holds its gates.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/assemble.rs
in: trust
find: .project(&root.project_key(), inner.person.verifier().as_ref()).ok()
replace: .project(&root.project_key(), inner.person.verifier().as_ref()).ok().filter(|_| false)
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it signed::under_trust_project_without_the_key_a_pinned_hooks_gate_holds
    cineris-core::it signed::under_trust_project_without_the_key_a_pinned_extensions_gate_holds

[break] trust-project-builds-no-uncounted
rule: An entry that does not count holds the gates of the extensions it pins whether the project is not trusted or trusted for the run by --trust-project.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/assemble.rs
in: assemble
find: let uncounted = stored.as_ref().and_then(crate::ext::found::Uncounted::of);
replace: let uncounted = stored.as_ref().filter(|_| !projects_looked_in).and_then(crate::ext::found::Uncounted::of);
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it signed::under_trust_project_without_the_key_a_pinned_extensions_gate_holds

[break] trust-project-hook-of-an-uncounted-entry-runs-or-lapses
rule: In a project trusted for the run, a hook the entry pins, where the entry does not count, is on its event, failing.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hooks.rs
in: in_session
find: let uncounted = stored.filter(|entry| entry.has_entry() && !entry.is_trusted());
replace: let uncounted = stored.filter(|_| false);
caught-by:
    cineris-core ext::hooks::tests::under_trust_project_a_hook_an_entry_that_does_not_count_pins_holds_its_event
    cineris-core::it signed::under_trust_project_without_the_key_a_pinned_hooks_gate_holds

# ---------------------------------------- the user's pins that do not count

[break] uncounted-pins-gone-hold-nothing
rule: While the user's pins do not count, an extension they pin that is gone is still found missing, and holds its gates.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/pipeline.rs
